      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re naming: Let me keep this name.\n\nNaming from the `fdt_overlay_target_offset()`, and `strip_overlay_(path_)prefix()` seems like a string operation, but API parses path to build valid and simplified path.\n\n-----\n\nRe simplifying code: I would do, but with different approach because stripping until `__overlay__` node isn\u0027t trivial.\n\nLet me explain with your code snippet.\n\n```\nlet chars \u003d path.to_bytes_with_nul();\nif !chars.starts_with(b\"/\") {\n   return Err(...);\n}\n\nlet mut chars_iter \u003d chars[1..].iter();\nlet fragment_len \u003d chars_iter.position(|c| *c \u003d\u003d b\u0027/\u0027).ok_or(...)?;\nlet overlay_len \u003d chars_iter.position(|c| *c \u003d\u003d b\u0027/\u0027).ok_or(...)?;\nlet prefix_len \u003d b\"/\".len() + fragment_len + overlay_len;\nlet (overlay_path, target_path) \u003d chars.split_at(prefix_len + 1);\n```\n\nThis code doesn\u0027t work. `libfdt` allows consecutive `/`, so `/////fragment@a/__overlay__/node_a` is the same as `/fragment@a/__overlay__/node_a`. So we can\u0027t simply count `/` to get node name at certain depth.\n\nIn other word, `fragment_len` and `overlay_len` may be incorrect. I need extra logic for the calculation.\n\nSo let me remove providing more precise path buffer size with `Vec::with_capacity()`.  It may allocate bit more bytes, but it would simplify code.\n\n-----\n\nRe Return:\nLet me keep this.\n\nI can change to return `\u0026CStr`, but two issues (may not be a blocker)\n  - Issue1: Code looks dirtier because I need handwritten tokenizer to get subslice from the `overlay_node_path`.\n  - Issue2: Technically this is getting overlay target path, but only allows `target-path \u003d \"/\"`. It\u0027s coincident that `\u0026CStr` can be returned for the result, but there could be extra prefix in general.\n\nJust FYI, here\u0027s my hand-written tokenizer to return `\u0026CStr`. Tell me if you prefer this style.\n\n```\n        /// \"target-path\" validation is the same.\n        \n        let overlay_node_name_bytes \u003d Self::OVERLAY_NODE_NAME.to_bytes();\n        let len \u003d overlay_node_path_bytes.len();\n        let (mut pos, mut depth) \u003d (0, 0);\n        while depth \u003c 2 \u0026\u0026 pos \u003c len {\n            while pos \u003c len \u0026\u0026 overlay_node_path_bytes[pos] \u003d\u003d b\u0027/\u0027\n                pos +\u003d 1;\n            }\n            depth +\u003d 1;\n            let name_start_pos \u003d pos;\n            while pos \u003c len \u0026\u0026 overlay_node_path_bytes[pos] !\u003d b\u0027/\u0027 {\n                pos +\u003d 1;\n            }\n            if depth \u003d\u003d 2 \u0026\u0026 overlay_node_path_bytes[name_start_pos..pos] !\u003d overlay_node_name_bytes {\n                return Err(DeviceAssignmentError::InvalidDtbo);\n            }\n        }\n                \n        Ok(CStr::from_bytes_with_nul(overlaid_node_path_bytes[pos..]).unwrap());\n```",
