      "message": "\u003e Re naming: Let me keep this name.\n\nCan you at least give it an \"action\" name? The current name is very confusing.\n\n\u003e So we can\u0027t simply count `/` to get node name at certain depth.\n\nThe DT spec implies that having consecutive `/` ins\u0027t compliant and `libfdt` probably supports it for backward-compatibility reasons (from the Open Firmware days). In particular, these paths are generated by DTC (as opposed to being hand-written) so are very unlikely to contain consecutive `/`.\n\n\u003e It\u0027s coincident that `\u0026CStr` can be returned for the result, but there could be extra prefix in general.\n\nFair enough; agreed regarding the return type.",
