      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T10:19:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Ping me if new name is still not-so-good.\n\nI\u0027m puzzled by it (`estimate_asssigned_device_node_path`) as no estimation is being performed by the function but whatever. Could you at least fix the typo in it?\n\n---\n\n\u003e How does DT spec say exactly?\n\nHere\u0027s what it says:\n\u003e _A node in the devicetree can be uniquely identified by specifying the full path from the root node, through all descendant nodes, to the desired node._\n\u003e\n\u003e _The convention for specifying a device path is:_\n\u003e ```\n\u003e /node-name-1/node-name-2/node-name-N\n\u003e ```\n\nand\n\n\u003e _Each node in the devicetree is named according to the following convention:_\n\u003e ```\n\u003e node-name@unit-address\n\u003e ```\n\u003e _The node-name component specifies the name of the node. It shall be 1 to 31 characters in length and consist solely of characters from the set of characters in Table 2.1._\n\nso the empty string isn\u0027t a valid `node-name-N` and valid paths don\u0027t contain consecutive `/`.\n\n---\n\n\u003e\u003e In particular, these paths are generated by DTC (as opposed to being hand-written) so are very unlikely to contain consecutive /.\n\u003e\n\u003e I\u0027m bit confused here.\n\nAll I\u0027m saying is that virtually all VM DTBOs will have been generated from a DTS by `dtc` (as opposed to being written by hand), which doesn\u0027t generate paths with consecutive `/` ([source code](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/eb747762bdd1889e4d65eae868f11c8cde3a8d7c:external/dtc/livetree.c;l\u003d877;drc\u003deb747762bdd1889e4d65eae868f11c8cde3a8d7c)).\n\nBut my overall point was that you\u0027re making this harder for yourself than necessary.",
