      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you be specific about your proposal?\n\nIn patchset #3 at https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/2792452/comment/fb0380ba_56f918df/, you recommended the same -- filter unsued node/props in ctor.\n\nBut when we discussed via VC, you proposed to modify `vm_dtbo` in `fdt.rs`\u0027s `patch()`. Here\u0027s the copy from our discussion note.\n\n```\nparse() {\n   let device_info \u003d DeviceInfo::new_filtered(fdt, vm_dtbo);  // vm_dtbo wouldn\u0027t be modified here.\n}\n\npatch() {\n  device_info.prepare_for_overlay(vm_dtbo);\n  fdt.apply_overlay(vm_dtbo);\n  device_info.patch(fdt);\n}\n```\n\nAnd it seems like that you\u0027re proposing earlier proposal again. Am I understanding correctly?\n\nTo be crystal clear, could you share your thoughts about where to filter unused nodes / properties? My preference is to do so in `DeviceAssignmentInfo::new()`, called by `parse_device_tree()` in `fdt.rs`.",
